cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this software or computational workflow, please cite it as below."

type: software

title: "Comparative models for heart disease prediction"

version: "1.0.1"

date-released: "2026-10-07"

authors:
  - given-names: "David Eduardo"
    family-names: "León"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7339-0068"

abstract: >
  Reproducible computational analysis accompanying the doctoral thesis
  and scientific article on the comparative evaluation of logistic
  regression, Random Forest, and Gradient Boosting models for heart
  disease prediction using the Cleveland Heart Disease Dataset. The
  computational workflow evaluates predictive performance, sensitivity,
  specificity, ROC AUC, calibration, stability, repeated stratified
  cross-validation, statistical inference, and independent test-set
  performance.

keywords:
  - "heart disease"
  - "machine learning"
  - "logistic regression"
  - "Random Forest"
  - "Gradient Boosting"
  - "predictive models"
  - "cross-validation"
  - "ROC AUC"
  - "clinical prediction"
  - "reproducible research"

